    "quote": "Under Assumption~\\ref{assump:linear_bandit_sugaussian}, we choose a linear reward model $f(\\xb,\\btheta)=\\xb^{\\top}\\btheta$ in Algorithm~\\ref{alg:ts_lmc_general}. Let $\\delta\\in(0,1)$. ... Then with probability $1-\\delta$, it holds that R(T)\\leq CRd\\log(1/\\delta)\\sqrt{dT\\log^3(1+T/(\\lambda d))}, where $C>0$ is an absolute constant that is independent of the problem."
